WEBVTT

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.320
Sorry, Alex.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.950
I'm too busy to pay 
attention to you today.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.420
I hope Squiddie gets here soon.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.410
Oh. Sounds like she's already here.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.350
Hang on!

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.630
I'm coming!

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.580
<b>How About A Squiddle Walk?!</b>

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.430
Come on in!

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:05.660
Hi.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.390
Huh?

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.850
Squiddie, you're wearing...

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.630
Squiderific, huh?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.320
Eiko gave me this hat 
and these sandals.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.490
Squiddie... You are so adorable!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.650
Squid it a rest!

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.410
Let me go!

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.480
Stop it! Untentacle me!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.420
Why the squid is your dog biting me?!

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.230
I'm really sorry.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.090
He doesn't normally bite.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.360
He's jealous.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.080
Huh?

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:42.550
It probably pissed him off to see 
you hanging on Squid Girl.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.560
This isn't good.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.520
If Squiddie doesn't like Alex, she won't 
want to come over anymore.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:54.730
Maybe you should get Squid Girl to walk Alex.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:58.900
I think it would help them bond.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.150
Yeah, huh.

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.360
That's a good idea!

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.890
Yeah, leave me alone with him

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:05.530
and it'll be an all-he-can-bite buffet!

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.970
No, it won't.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:11.120
Each bite is one meal down the drain.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.340
Did that dog understand that?

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.520
You can just let him lead the way.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.920
Take care!

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.970
What, I don't get the squidding right to refuse?!

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.140
A big dog's coming this way.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:33.650
Why are you...?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.160
There's no way you can win a 
fight against a dog that big!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.610
Come back here!

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.050
He acted all tough, now he's 
shivering like kelp on a current.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.740
What a useless dog.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.120
It's a tiny dog.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.550
I guess this time he won't get scared.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.470
Kelp has more backbone than you.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.350
What the heck are you doing?!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.160
Does this dog actually understand Japanese?

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.110
He's kind of creepy.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.010
So, which way should we go?

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.210
This way?

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:38.290
I think Sanae trusts 
Alex a squiddle too much.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.110
Jeez.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:45.050
What a stubborn, scaredy, 
dopey, floundering dog.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.720
I think I just described myself.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.180
What do you say, Alex?

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.800
If you get stuck, you can just go back.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.750
You can't let something 
like this pull you under.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.680
If you keep a positive outlook on life,

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.240
there's sure to be something so exsquidsite

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.820
that you'll forget all the bad things!

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:08.700
I guess there's no way you, 
as a dog, can understand that.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.510
It'll be quite a long walk,

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.030
but I ink we can take our time 
retracing our steps.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.040
All right, here we go!

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:21.060
Get it!

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.190
Wow, that was tentastic!

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.810
Do you want to try too?

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.370
I just need to find something to throw.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.690
I've got the perfect thing!

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.910
I'm going to throw this sandal 
and you have to catch it.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.300
Why aren't you fetching?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.950
I'm trying to toughen you up!

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.960
Go fetch! Now!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.860
Hey! Hurry up!

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.840
What the squid do you think you're doing?!

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.720
You're going in there and bringing 
my squidding sandal right back!

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.570
He's taking forever.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.180
What's he doing in there?

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.830
Alex, are you okay?

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.010
Come on, let's jet!

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.510
You're back for more?

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:57.730
Back off, unless you want to 
further feel my tentacles' wrath!

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:00.730
Why you...!

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.610
Stop it!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.430
What are you doing?

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.740
Give it back!

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.160
Oh no! My sandal!

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:19.540
Alex!

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.460
Good job, Alex!

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.530
Now it's time to say good-bye.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.180
You were pretty great back there.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.840
I've changed my mind about you.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.060
Huh? Thank you.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.270
My sandal...

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.200
That's okay.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.900
I know you didn't do it out of malice.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.780
Let's go home!

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.000
What on earth happened to you?

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.210
You're all scratched up!

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.670
You could say a lot happened.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.380
Alex, you're all banged up!

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.850
You're all banged up!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.470
Squiddie, are you all right?

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.430
Look, you're all red here.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.270
I'll get you some ointment right away.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.280
Those are just squiddle scratches.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.970
Poor Squiddie!

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.520
Let me go!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.820
You're not listening!

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:32.490
These are...

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.950
Owwww!

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:38.870
What the squid are you doing?!

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:43.210
I guess just going for a walk 
together wasn't enough.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:56.210
It's nice to walk early in the 
morning now and then.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.980
What are all those listless 
squiddle kids doing here?

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.750
What are they up to at this hour?

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:14.070
<b>Time To Squidzercise?!</b>

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.120
To start off, we're going to face the sun

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.830
and give him a big "Good morning."

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.500
What the squid is this?

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:26.160
Now gently roll your bodies side to side...

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.540
Three, four.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.200
Say "I'm sorry."

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:32.450
Now be a bigshot.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.250
"I won't do it again."

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.420
"Just kidding."

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:42.290
Meow, meow, meow, meow, you're a cat!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.660
Chase the foxtail!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.650
Now chase it like you mean it!

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.920
You sense someone behind you 
at an angle! Swing wide at him!

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.980
Never mind, it was just your imagination.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:55.760
Now he's on your other side! Swing wide!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:00.270
Crawl in place.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.800
Crawl in place, double time!

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:05.550
As fast as you can!

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:09.800
Avoid hyperventilating.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.510
Breathe deep.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.650
Are they done?

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.120
What do those movements mean, anyway?

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.580
And now, let's say "Good 
Morning" to the land!

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.390
They're starting again!

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.860
Look like an old lady with a bent back.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:34.230
"Saturday Night... Hermit."

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:38.290
"Friday Night... Shut-In."

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.310
Crab, crab, crab, crab.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.030
Do the Crab-Walk.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.000
Now the Gadding-Around Crab Walk!

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.960
Now let's see "Crying makes you tough."

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.630
And "The Back-Itch."

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.210
And "The Scarecrow's Got a Soul."

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.130
"Come Here, Come Here. Now, Get Lost."

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:02.740
Is this some kind of ritual?

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:03.810
A form of brain-washing?

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.350
Make sure you watch your breathing.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:08.100
Is this the "Weird Dance" that steals MP?

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.120
Deep breath.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.730
I guess now they're really done.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.020
I have no idea what they were just doing,

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:20.610
but they look so much happier now 
than when they came down here.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.660
I ink those strange moves

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:26.240
must have some kind of secret power.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.540
Lemon

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:31.010
The oil noodles and fried 
pork cutlet are ready.

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:32.000
Thank you.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.580
Fried noodles for table 5!

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.540
Please take that one, Squid Girl.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.760
Okay.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.400
I can't get that squidding song from 
this morning out of my head.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:45.140
What were those poses again?

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:49.640
I remember one that looked like this.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.950
You're communicating with 
aliens, aren't you?

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:56.740
No, I'm not!

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:59.750
What was that? Some kind of transmission?

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:57.980
Hey, Squid Girl.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:58.880
Get back to work.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.860
I know, I know!

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:00.860
Huh? Huh? Huh?!

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.700
One moment, please.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.780
I ink one went like this, too.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:09.970
What is she doing?

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.040
A new ability?

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.380
That's so gross!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.090
There was also something like this.

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:18.890
Oh, my god!

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:21.050
What are all these super-pretty 
moves you're doing?

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.110
"Come here, come here..."

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.550
"Leap into my arms"?!

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:29.280
Squiddie, you've changed 
your mind about me.

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:31.290
I love you, Squid-!

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.590
Hey!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.540
Get back to work already!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:36.410
Oh, yeah!

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.070
There was one like this too.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.780
And a much bigger one.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.500
Hey, that really squidding hurt!

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.030
What are you doing?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.170
You totally provoked me!

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:54.040
Stop screwing around 
and bring over that ramen.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:55.790
Fine.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:59.810
There were all these other poses too.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.170
Now I remember!

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:05.130
Behind you at an angle, swing wide...

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:10.870
I'm so squiddy sorry!

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.890
It wasn't on purpose!

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.850
And then there was that one where

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:20.070
you stand like this and 
then move around like so.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.110
Looks like you're not really sorry...

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.270
That's unfortunate...

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.390
No, you've got it all wrong!

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:28.070
I just drifted into the next pose!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.050
I guess I really can't work like this.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.950
All I can think about is those squidding moves.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:37.660
I'm going to watch them 
again tomorrow morning.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.070
Good morning, everybody!

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:47.190
Good morning.

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:49.560
Let's start our exercises 
so we can face the day!

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:52.810
There's some girl I've never seen before.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.530
Oh well, this activity is free to all, I guess.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.300
And now, let's start!

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.660
We're going to face the sun and 
give him a big "Good morning."

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:10.730
Now gently roll your bodies side to side.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.560
Say "I'm sorry."

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.080
Now be a bigshot.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:19.490
"I won't do it again."

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.950
"Just kidding."

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:27.260
Meow, meow, meow, meow, you're a cat!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.050
Is everyone keeping up?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.760
What happened here?

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:35.420
Make sure you watch your breathing.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.430
Deep breath...

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.190
And that's it!

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.250
Now I get it.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.200
Just five minutes of 
moving your body around

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.660
can make you feel so buoyant.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:53.140
Now everybody grab your 
attendance cards and line up.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.620
Attendance cards?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:55.340
Here you go.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.920
Thank you.

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:59.080
This is your first time here, isn't it?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:03.090
Radio Calisthenics

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:00.760
Here you are.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.090
I put a stamp for today.

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.950
I got stamped!

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.470
What will I be expected to 
squidrifice for the sake of my health?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.510
It's not that kind of stamp.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.940
So you're saying that if I get the entire 
sheet stamped, I get a prize?

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:18.810
Yup.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.440
When I turned it in last year,
 I got a lot of candy.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.500
Squiii!

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.190
I'm going to get a prize too!

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.660
Now everybody grab your 
attendance cards and line up.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.550
I'd like my prize.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:35.410
Already?

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.120
<b>Aizawa, Aizawa, Aizawa, Aizawa...</b>

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.680
Please don't come again.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.790
But why?!

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:45.880
<b>Aizawa</b>

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.040
Squid Girlie...

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:55.890
What's wrong?

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.210
Our ball went all the way out there.

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.320
Just do that thing and get it.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:09.230
I guess there's squiddle else I can do.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.240
What is this?!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.060
Here you go.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:21.940
Thanks!

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.210
Hey, Squid Girl.

00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:30.660
Oh, it's you, Goro?

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:33.090
Have you ever considered 
becoming a lifeguard?

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:39.390
<b>Wanna Lend A Helping Tentacle?!</b>

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.220
Me... a lifeguard?

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:43.690
Yeah.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.150
When saving people from the ocean, 
speed is really important.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:50.610
Your tentacles would be the fastest 
way to get to a drowning person.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:54.840
This ocean would become totally 
safe with you as a lifeguard.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:55.280
That's why, I...

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:57.280
That sounds like a lot of squidding work.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.990
Of course, it wouldn't be for free.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.950
Yuigahama Lifeguard Pavilion

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.180
What do you say?

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.420
You'd get a lunch like 
this each time you work.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.000
Fried shrimp!

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:11.050
You're looking at Chizuru's special 
lunch box, so you know it's good!

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:14.540
Lemon doesn't make lunch boxes like this.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.850
She'll make them to order, if she has time.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.510
I didn't know that.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.870
You don't have to eat it if you don't want it.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.250
You're going to just give 
her that lunch box? But...

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.930
The truth is...

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:31.570
I really want to eat it!

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.990
But I'll use it to get her 
to become a lifeguard.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.530
That's really squidilicious!

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:40.990
You're eating it... now?

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.200
I'm really full now.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.890
Thank you.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.580
Hey! Wait right there!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:54.010
Since you ate every last bite, 
I guess that means you'll do it.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:55.730
Do what?

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:57.340
You ate it without intending to do it?!

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:59.790
A lifeguard, huh?

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:04.100
Ask me anything you want to know.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:07.390
Do I have to get a tan, too?

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.000
It's not like it's a uniform!!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.190
It's the lifeguard's job to look 
after the swimmers' safety.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.530
Let's start with the patrol.

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.240
Patrol?

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.360
For example...

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.460
You've got too many 
people on that raft!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.780
Take turns when you use it!

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:31.920
Yes, sir.

00:18:32.390 --> 00:18:34.280
That's what you've got to do.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.060
So I just need to warn them.

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:37.980
Yup.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:39.840
Sounds like a snap.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.140
I don't like shrimp.

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:45.810
Leaving a perfectly good 
shrimp is such a waste!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.230
Sheesh.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.330
That doesn't mean you can eat it!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:57.530
If you value your life,
 get away from him right now!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:02.320
Don't spoil peoples' fun!

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.560
That'll krill him!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.620
I told you, they're just having fun!

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.300
Take that!

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.750
Stop it!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.590
No means no!

00:19:15.260 --> 00:19:17.370
You've got to consider 
the whole picture.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.300
Consider the whole picture!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.930
Can't something be done 
about all this trash?

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.390
This is part of the job, too.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:35.110
I always say that the ocean 
isn't a trash can...

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:38.580
Are the humans incapable of learning?

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.630
Polluting the ocean is the 
worst kind of offense.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.500
You can't get in the squidding water!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:57.250
Why not?

00:19:57.490 --> 00:20:00.150
Just get out, right now!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.080
Hey, what are you doing?

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:07.350
I told you, our job is to

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.140
look after the swimmers' safety, 
not get in their way!

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.810
But I'm keeping them safe!

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.290
How, may I ask?

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.180
You're just getting in their way!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:20.340
Our job is to keep the ocean safe.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:22.310
Don't you understand that?

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.950
I get it!

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:25.730
No, you obviously don't!

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:28.450
If you got it, why did you chase 
those boys out of the water?

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.160
You did it because you hate 
humans for polluting the water!

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:36.540
Of course it makes this squid angry 
when people pollute the water.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:39.630
The ocean is what I'm here to protect.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:46.260
Throwing something like this in 
the ocean is bad for its health.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:50.140
I thought you and I were on the same page.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:54.150
That's enough. I shouldn't have asked you.

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:59.860
What's Goro getting all upset about?

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:04.610
You were right. She couldn't do the job.

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:08.180
Saving people isn't all about your abilities.

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:11.210
It's about how strong your desire 
to save someone is.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.830
Help!

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:17.730
Let's go, Isozaki!

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.340
Okay!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:21.090
Hang on!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:22.550
We're coming to save you!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.760
It's no use.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:30.100
We're not going to make it!

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:44.670
Thank you so much for saving our boys.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.740
Thanks, Squid Girlie!

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:50.620
You shouldn't be swimming out so deep
 if you don't have tentacles!

00:21:50.840 --> 00:21:51.920
Jeez.

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:53.540
Too bad, huh?

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:56.160
She could really be the best lifeguard.

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.970
No, I was wrong.

00:21:58.970 --> 00:21:59.710
Huh?

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:02.380
She's always watching over everyone,

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:04.630
Be more careful next time.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:06.590
whether she's officially a lifeguard or not.

00:22:05.170 --> 00:22:06.400
Okay.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.080
Then fine!

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:42.440
How are you all doing?

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:45.320
I'm doing great! 
Takeru Aizawa here!

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.440
Next time will be:

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:47.820
"Squidn't that English?!"

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:48.860
"Ink you can stop it?!"

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:50.120
"Get my drift?!"

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.160
All three!

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:53.430
Enjoy!
